cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Aorta mesh-morphing haemodynamics pipeline
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this record) and the
  associated article listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
abstract: >-
  Boundary-condition generation and parameter calibration for patient-specific
  thoracic-aorta haemodynamics, where the computational domain follows wall
  kinematics measured in the patient rather than a wall material model. Covers
  inlet velocity from 4D flow MRI, wall motion by radial-basis-function morphing,
  Windkessel outlet calibration and wall-stiffness calibration. Also includes the
  cine-CTA wall-motion tracking step that supplies the measured kinematics,
  published here for the first time. A wholly synthetic example executes and
  quantitatively checks the wall-morphing stage. Patient-derived inputs are not
  distributed; solver configurations are neutral, non-runnable templates.
  Segmentation and volumetric meshing are upstream and not included. This release
  covers the aorta-mesh-morphing component of the AneurysmTool project repository,
  which is its entire content at this version.
# The software author list is not the article's, and is ordered to make that
